    "result_text": "The full suite is green. `BUILD SUCCESS` with the acceptance test (the only test class) passing, including the new `coreComputesInitials` check for `J.S.`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an `initials` field to the owner API following the exact pattern already established for `displayName`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (`Owner` schema) \u2014 declared a new read-only `initials` string property, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes it and it's serialized in the owner JSON.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(formatInitials(owner))\")` and a small `formatInitials` default method that returns the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `\"J.S.\"`).\n\nThe initials logic lives alongside `formatDisplayName` in the mapper \u2014 the same single-responsibility unit that already owns deriving presentation fields from an `Owner`'s stored names \u2014 rather than being duplicated or dropped into a controller/entity.",
